{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99868","id":2208249923,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6DnzhD","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99868","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99868.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99868.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99868","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99868/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99868/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99868/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e839cf44f55d438112fc9e82983d890bf759494a","number":99868,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Allow non-tres text resources (for GDScript and C# currently) to store metadata","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The problem comes from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99748#issuecomment-2504004205\r\nAfter days of work, I finally figured out a solution.\r\n\r\n# `.gdmeta` file\r\nLike `.uid` files, `.gdmeta` files are actually resuffixed config files (sorry but I don't know how to parse a format data file in a better way...), which is placed in the same directory as the resource files. When a text resource (referring to a resource that is stored directly with its texts) contains metadata and is going to store its data, a `.gdmeta` file will be created in the same directory of the resource file. When a resource has no metadata while its metadata file exists, the metadata file will be removed.\r\n\r\n# Metadata files for `GDScript` and `C#`\r\nCurrently, this PR only supports GDScript and C# to store metadata files, and the other types of text resources will be allowed soon by future PRs of mine or other contributors.\r\nIn their definitions of formatters' `save()` and `load()`, there will be `save_meta()` and `load_meta()` respectively in the middle-bottom of the method body, which are defined in `ResourceFormatSaver` and `ResourceFormatLoader` correspondingly.\r\n\r\n# Limitations\r\nCurrently, I'm not sure whether the method `load_meta()` should be written like that, or should be written with the background of multi-thread programming (i.e. `Mutex` or something else for multi-thread work). If you have better solution, feel free to share yours in this pr. :)\r\n\r\n# WIPs\r\n- [x] Add `.gdmeta` file for storing metadatas of text resources, and add meta `save_meta()` and `load_meta()` for operations of the file.\r\n- [x] Allow `GDScript` and `C#` script resources to store metadata.\r\n- [ ] Local test and feedback solution.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"arc